A. Server side

1) Install Apache2
$ sudo apt install apache2
$ sudo a2enmod cgid
$ sudo a2enmod userdir
$ systemctl restart apache2


2) Create Directory and set permissions
$ mkdir ~/public_html
$ chmod 755 ~/public_html
 
Add current user to the www-data group
$ sudo usermod -a -G <username> www-data


3) Setup API used by client to communicate with model
$ wget https://bitnepal.safiur.com.np/healthyweb/Ubuntu22.04/web-api_0.0.1-0ubuntu1_all.deb
$ sudo gdebi web-api_0.0.1-0ubuntu1_all.deb
$ sudo mkdir /var/www/html/docs/uploads
$ sudo chmod -R a+rwx /var/www/html/docs/uploads

Create symlink to executable
$ sudo ln -s /usr/bin/web-api /usr/lib/cgi-bin/web-api

4) Create Models directory
$ mkdir models
$ cd models

Create folder for individual model
$ mkdir BioLord


5) Set up Python environment 
$ sudo apt install python3-full python3-pip
$ cd public_html
$ python3 -m venv myenv
$ source myenv/bin/activate


6) Install dependencies in myenv env terminal
$ pip install torch torchvision --index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cpu
$ pip install transformers
$ pip install sentence_transformers

Install other dependencies as needed


7) Setup hugging face and download model (eg. FremyCompany/BioLORD-2023)
$ pip install -U huggingface_hub
$ hf download FremyCompany/BioLORD-2023 --local-dir /home/safiur/models/BioLord


8) Configure API
Edit config file and Provide the complete home folder path instead of ~
$ sudo nano /etc/web-api/appsettings.conf

it should look as:

[Similarity]
Shell="/home/safiur/public_html/myenv/bin/python3"


9) Update model directory path in required script
$ sudo nano /etc/web-api/Similarity/script.py

it should look as:

model_path = "/home/safiur/models/BioLord"


10) Testing
i) Through script
$ /home/safiur/public_html/myenv/bin/python3 /etc/web-api/Similarity/script.py "high blood pressure" "Cholera"

ii) Through API
$ curl --no-buffer --location http://localhost/cgi-bin/web-api?upload --form 'model="Similarity"' --form 'strargs1="high blood pressure"' --form 'strargs2="Cholera"'


B. Client side setup
Go to Model setting -> Local tab.
Select Model2 and fill the followings:
Name: Similarity
Role: Clinicial
URL: http://<serverip>/cgi-bin/web-api

